{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018237-playing-music-during-sessions","id":1018237,"title":"Playing music during sessions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-16T15:36:09-08:00","id":1018237,"title":"Playing music during sessions","content":"Has anyone ever successfully used music to create some sort of atmosphere during your sessions? I've tried but I always feel like it's just distracting.<br /> <br /> Any advice? For choosing music, as well as for when to use it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12761-suzuki","name":"Suzuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T15:44:20-08:00","id":1018240,"title":"","content":"Use OST music! Non-vocal ones makes players least distracted. Alternatively, mostly instrumental music also works.<br /> <br /> And think about games or movies that convey the feel you want to share with players. When I run <b>Mage</b> I use <i>Tomb Raider</i> games OST to uncovering Ruins of Time Before, band Arcana and <i>Battlestar Galactica</i> OST for general mood of Mysteries in game and <i>Call of Cthulhu: Dark Corners of The Earth</i> OST for Abyss and Paradox feel, for example. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Think about scenes you want to show - then think about movies and games having similar - and steal their OST for session. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T16:38:32-08:00","id":1018258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suzuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018237-playing-music-during-sessions#post1018237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone ever successfully used music to create some sort of atmosphere during your sessions? I've tried but I always feel like it's just distracting.<br /> <br /> Any advice? For choosing music, as well as for when to use it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Find the volume that works best, err on the side of it being low. Primarily, it's stronger and more important when establishing a scene, a mood, an attitude, and when you get into the particulars, it's better for it to go down.<br /> <br /> Music depends on the scenes, but keep in mind that vocals will often be ignored-if the song is likable and appropriate, use it anyways, but instrumentals go farther than not. Exceptions exist in when you know the song has a particular meaning for someone-the Music is Always section of Mage the Awakening Second Edition should be used in any game where you want to use music, because it invites players to give you songs and meanings to use as cues, and if you know a group has a response to a song (particularly with vocals), exploit the fuck out of it.<br /> <br /> Music humanizes as a general rule, particularly when it has vocals. Some songs do great for capturing the alien and the other, but by and large, you should think about how music reveals the nature and tenor of a things &quot;humanity&quot;.I don't mean humanity as an inherent trait, but in that which the audience can see themselves in, how humanity projects themselves onto things.<br /> <br /> Combat music is better being brutal and heavy rather than fast and vicious. Fast and vicious will just annoy people.<br /> <br /> Those are some general guidelines I've found work. Mostly, it's a matter of feeling out your group and what works.<br /> <br /> There is one hard rule to using music in games:<br /> <br /> The King in Yellow grooves to Call Me Maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T17:10:11-08:00","id":1018266,"title":"","content":"I use non-vocals for background ambience, but to introduce plots and themes, I very often use songs. Part of the setting lore our group has worked up is that there's a phantom station called &quot;The Radio.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>The Radio Knows</b><br /> Listen to the radio. Turned off, unplugged, switched to tape or CD, not even capable of picking up anything other than AM? It still knows. It plays music, old reports, numbers stations, desperate cries for help. Once you're exposed to the supernatural, the radio speaks out. Maybe it's that music is the soul of humanity, or that music is some kind of universal language, our response to threats from within and without to face them with bald commentary that no one in power has ever really noticed. Regardless, nearby radios will always know something appropriate. You can even call in. The announcer is more than happy to talk. While you wait on The Somber Grounds of Truth, you might feel an Overnight Sensation, begging you to take One Shot at Glory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T17:12:50-08:00","id":1018267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suzuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018237-playing-music-during-sessions#post1018237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone ever successfully used music to create some sort of atmosphere during your sessions? I've tried but I always feel like it's just distracting.<br /> <br /> Any advice? For choosing music, as well as for when to use it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I pretty much use music in every session of my games, but I'm careful about choice. I almost always use ambient / minimalist music, without vocals, unless I'm doing something where the music is meant to be diagetic, or if I'm doing what you might call an &quot;HBO moment&quot;. I make an exception to that for fights, because so often it's people waiting around to take a turn, so I don't mind if it's a little more high energy, and / or distracting.<br /> <br /> I have a few albums of ambient music I rely on, though it can depend on the game I'm running. Boards of Canada works well for <b>Demon </b>and <b>Mage</b>, whereas Bohren &amp; der Club of Gore works well for <b>Vampire</b>. I also use the <i>Bloodlines </i>soundtrack, <i>a lot</i>. I do have some other standbys (Fennesz + Sakamoto are great for setting a slightly melancholic, creepy tone).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T11:24:23-08:00","id":1019870,"title":"","content":"I do. For almost all of my games. The chase music in Silent Hill Shattered Memories was particularly great when the group were being chased through the Hedge by a Huntsman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}